# Qoduck — findings by GLM 5.3 Flash

- Source: Alibaba Qoder (`qoduck` — stealth, no API identifier)
- Date: 2026-11-11 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> SELF-EXCLUDED — zero verified public benchmark numbers found for this model after a full pass over Qoder's official event documentation, an independent architecture analysis, news coverage and the models.dev/Hugging Face registries (no official entry anywhere). Qoduck is a stealth model with no model card, no published weights, no API identifier and no vendor-published benchmark — any score would be a placeholder. Verified facts recorded below for future re-research if Alibaba names it.

## Model card

- **Name:** Qoduck
- **Short description:** Alibaba Qoder's stealth coding model (Nov 2026) — identity undisclosed by the vendor; offered free inside a daily allowance to individual Qoder users for a limited time. Community guesses (Qwen4-27B with an n-gram lookup table) are unverified; the only firm fact is Qoder's own "stealth model whose identity has yet to be disclosed".
- **Provider / access:** Qoder app model picker only (Qoder CN and Qoder International, individual accounts — Free/Pro/Pro+/Ultra plans and membership cards); IDE, JetBrains plugin and CLI excluded from the promo; Teams/Enterprise accounts do not see the model. No public API endpoint — cannot be called from user code.
- **Release / knowledge:** appeared 2026-11-07 (Beijing/Singapore time); the free promo ran to 2026-11-11 10:00 (UTC+8), after which Qoder stated Qoduck "will be removed when the promotion ends". Knowledge cutoff unknown.
- **IDs:** none published — no API identifier, no weights repo; not listed in models.dev or the official Qwen Hugging Face org.
- **Context window:** Not announced — no vendor-published context figure (a 1M-token claim circulating on social media is unverified; the independent OrcaRouter analysis explicitly lists "no context figure" among unpublished facts).
- **Modalities:** Text in / text out in practice (coding product); nothing official — no modality documentation exists.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-11):** free within a daily allowance during the promo (Credit rate 0.5× → 0.0×, including at highest thinking intensity; does not draw the daily 100 general-purpose Credits); standard rate after the allowance is 0.5× — the same premium factor Qoder's consumption reference attaches to Qwen3.8-Max and DeepSeek-V4-Pro (Qwen3.8-Flash sits at 0.1×).
- **Architecture:** unverified. The leading community reading (35 GB at Q8 vs ~29–31 GB for Qwen3.8-27B FP8, implying +5–7B parameters, plausibly an n-gram lookup table like Qwen3.8-Flash-Next's 51B table on its 125B backbone, plus MTP; 480 tok/s second-hand) is hearsay — no rig, quant or run published; Alibaba's only written Qwen 4 statement (2026-09-22) says Qwen 4 is in training, not shipped.

## Deeper-source sweep (second pass, 2026-11-11)

- **Qoder International docs** (docs.qoder.com/events/qoduck-free) mirror the CN promotion exactly: Nov 7 → Nov 11, 2026 10:00 (UTC+8), daily free allowance, Credit rate 0.5× → 0.0× even at highest thinking intensity, individual plans only (Free, Pro Trial, Lite, Pro, Pro+, Ultra; Teams/Enterprise ineligible), Qoduck removed when the promotion ends. Both vendor surfaces confirm the same facts and neither names the model.
- **Operator entity:** the international docs footer names Bright Zenith Pte Ltd (© 2026) as Qoder International's operator; the CN docs name Tongyi Yunqi (Hangzhou) — both Alibaba-linked, consistent with the Qwen-family tokenizer evidence, but neither is a model-card statement.
- **Qoder changelog** (changelog.qoder.cn/en/qoder, through v0.5.7 on 2026-11-09): no Qoduck-specific entry, no capability or benchmark notes — the model exists only as a picker slot inside the promotion.
- Still no identity disclosure, no benchmark, no API identifier on any surface checked (both Qoder docs, changelog, OrcaRouter, news, models.dev, HF). The exclusion verdict is unchanged and now double-sourced on both vendor docs.

